From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flax <flax@tiogapass>
Date: Wed, 08 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: allow re-acquiring HttpPushUriTargetsBusy after failed update

After a failed BMC firmware update the httpPushUriTargetBusy global
stays true for the lifetime of the bmcweb process.  Without a BMC
reboot the next update attempt hits the resourceInUse guard and shows
"Error in switching running and backup images" in the WebUI.

Remove the exclusive-lock guard.  On a single-user embedded BMC there
is no concurrent-client scenario that requires it, and idempotent
re-acquisition (true->true) is always safe.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [single-platform workaround]
---
 redfish-core/lib/update_service.hpp | 8 --------
 1 file changed, 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/redfish-core/lib/update_service.hpp b/redfish-core/lib/update_service.hpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/redfish-core/lib/update_service.hpp
+++ b/redfish-core/lib/update_service.hpp
@@ -2162,14 +2162,6 @@ inline void handleUpdateServicePatch(

     if (imgTargetBusy)
     {
-        if ((httpPushUriTargetBusy) && (*imgTargetBusy))
-        {
-            BMCWEB_LOG_DEBUG(
-                "Other client has reserved the HttpPushUriTargets property for firmware updates.");
-            messages::resourceInUse(asyncResp->res);
-            return;
-        }
-
         if (imgTargets)
         {
             if (!(*imgTargetBusy))
